IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-electrical`

-- g7-tests-electrical.l4: tests of sections 58 and 61 (the licensee and the Electricity Law).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Expected values come from the SOURCE, decided before any run:
--   s.58  a holder of a licence under the Law is treated as a service electrician for cooling systems.  So: some
--         licence in force and the act is work on a cooling system gives TRUE; no licence in force gives FALSE; a
--         licence but an act that is not work on a cooling system gives FALSE ("for cooling systems").
--   s.61  the added subsection (e) of section 6 of the Electricity Law: electrical work in accordance with the First
--         Schedule, within work on a cooling system, by a person who holds a licence under the Law.  Three conditions,
--         each tested by dropping it alone.
--   T32   the discriminating case between the two: electrical work on a cooling system that the First Schedule does
--         not list.  Section 58 read widely lets the licensee do it, section 61 read as the only gateway does not.

§ `Tests of sections 58 and 61`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`no licence in force` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`a grade 1 licence in force` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`a grade 2 licence in force` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`a grade 3 licence in force` MEANS LIST `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`two licences in force` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`, `grade 3 licence`

§§ `Section 58`

-- Each licence kind gives the status: the Law's three kinds are all "a licence to perform work on a cooling system".
#ASSERT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `a grade 2 licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `a grade 3 licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `two licences in force` TRUE

-- No licence in force: not a licensee, so no deeming.
#ASSERT NOT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `no licence in force` TRUE

-- A licensee, but the act is not work on a cooling system: the deeming holds "for cooling systems" only.
#ASSERT NOT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `a grade 3 licence in force` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `no licence in force` FALSE

§§ `Section 61: the electrical work allowed by subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law`

-- All three conditions met: a licence in force, work on a cooling system, electrical work in accordance with the First Schedule.
#ASSERT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE TRUE

-- Each condition dropped alone.
#ASSERT NOT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `no licence in force` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `a grade 1 licence in force` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE FALSE

-- Every kind of licence reaches it.
#ASSERT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `a grade 2 licence in force` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `a grade 3 licence in force` TRUE TRUE

§§ `Section 58 against section 61 (trap T32, fork F-E-1)`

-- Electrical work that the First Schedule lists, done by a licensee on a cooling system: both readings open it.
#ASSERT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE TRUE

-- The discriminating case: electrical work on a cooling system that the First Schedule does not list (for
-- example work on an electrical system that is not the integral one).  Section 58 read widely: open.  Section 61
-- read as the only gateway: not open.  The two readings disagree, and the Law does not say which governs.
#ASSERT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` `a grade 1 licence in force` TRUE FALSE

-- No licence: neither reading opens it.
#ASSERT NOT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` `no licence in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` `no licence in force` TRUE TRUE
